{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>You shall not slaughter upon leavened bread the blood of my sacrifice.</b> Rashi explained: a warning to the slaughterer, or to the one who throws the blood, or to one of the members of the group. As is taught in the chapter Tamid: if one slaughtered the Paschal offering upon leavened bread, he transgresses a negative prohibition — when? At the time that the leavened bread belongs to the slaughterer, or to the one who throws the blood, or to one of the members of the group. He cited it by way of not having mentioned it above in the section of 'the sacrifice of the Pesach festival.'" "<b>And it shall not remain until morning.</b> Above, in the section Mishpatim, He warned concerning the fat portions, and here He warned concerning the flesh itself."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "פירש״י (Rashi's commentary) expanded as 'ר׳ שלמה יצחקי' per the compiler's reverent abbreviation style; שנאו ('he cited it') read as referring back to Rashi's act of citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:54.169554885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}